  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Single-phase fcc FeCoNi-based high-entropy alloys have high saturation magnetization.",
      "field": "hypothesis; material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline coercive field of single-phase fcc FeCoNi-based high-entropy alloys is typically below 100 Oe.",
      "field": "hypothesis; material_initial_state; baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Severe plastic deformation at greater than 70% strain will introduce a high density of dislocations in the alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis; conditions; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Severe plastic deformation followed by low-temperature annealing will introduce or retain a high density of twin boundaries in the alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis; structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A short anneal at approximately 400 °C can partially recover ductility without significantly reducing defect density.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dislocations and twin boundaries act as pinning sites for magnetic domain walls.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pinning by the introduced defects increases the field required for domain-wall motion or nucleation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The increased domain-wall pinning will enhance coercivity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will increase coercivity to approximately 200–300 Oe.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The treatment will maintain a high level of saturation magnetization while increasing coercivity.",
      "field": "hypothesis; predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Over-annealing can cause excessive softening or loss of the defect structure relevant to the intervention.",
      "field": "boundary; uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Processing may initiate unwanted phase transformations in single-phase fcc FeCoNi-based alloys.",
